  "description": "BILWAW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H100 Cl8 Gd4 Mn8 N8 O54,4(C1 H4 O1),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.824-3.903 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.21-130.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H128Cl8Gd4Mn8N8O64. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
